From cd8d5b4ebb01f73626f6ecdf81d205309bd6f2c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sb.*: off is off for the settings hash and the state version;
 child retries; its own marginals

From the review of PR 6:

- The sb.* keys are in the settings hash only when sb.depths is set (then all of
  them, defaults included). A run without it has the hash it had before the keys
  existed: the five settings.golden hashes are cognac's again, and a cognac state
  file resumes under this binary and back without --allow-settings-change.
- A state file is QAP-STATE 10 only once strong branching chose a line (a nonzero
  sb_*_level array); otherwise write_state and bench/parallel.py write version 9,
  the file they wrote before.
- A child's bound is never taken below the one it inherits: QPB's for it or the
  node's own DNN bound. With dnn.retry = 1 a child solve that fails that
  setting's test is solved again without the pool, then cold, each with sb.iters,
  and the best certified bound counts. QAP_SB_TRACE counts the children retried
  and those still failed; QAP_SB_PROGRESS lines end with the retry steps.
- The shortlist's marginals are the node's own vector (sb_xbar): dnn_xbar is
  filled under rules 8 and 9 only, as before, so est.xbar's dive weights and the
  rules see what they saw at nodes where strong branching does not choose.

Checked: nug20 with the nug30 recipe and no sb.depths, node trace, state version
and settings hash equal cognac 21dd774a's, and each binary resumes the other's
checkpoint; nug20 and nug22 with strong branching at depths 0 to 2, node traces
and strong-branching traces equal the previous commit's; make test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014vvMYV3r6FDoHTc2G3VVqC
